Day 52/100 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 199: (Binary Tree Right Side View) 
-Approach:
I used Depth-First Search (DFS) with recursion.
Traverse the tree by visiting the right child first, followed by the left child.
Keep track of the current depth.
Since we visit the right side first, the first node encountered at each depth is the node visible from the right side.
Add a node to the result only when we visit that depth for the first time.

-Time Complexity:
O(n)-Every node is visited at most once.
-Space Complexity:
O(h)-Due to the recursive call stack, where h is the height of the tree.
The output list can contain up to O(h) nodes.

-Key Learnings:
Today's problem helped me strengthen my understanding of:
1) Binary Trees
2) Depth-First Search (DFS)
3) Recursive traversal
4) Right-first traversal
5) Tracking nodes based on tree depth
